","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rule, ","type":"text"},{"code":"startFuse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" naming a daemon.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"fatalError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot be caught, so the only way to assert on one is to run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it in a child process and read what it printed. Swift Testing’s exit tests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"do the running; this does the reading:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let result = await #expect(processExitsWith: .failure, observing: [\\.standardErrorContent]) {","    _ = try await play(ProceedMisuseGame(), [\"take wrench\"])","}","expectTrap(result, says: \"proceed() was called twice\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A trap test fails in two very different ways and the message says which:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"nothing on stderr"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" means the process died before it could print, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a different message"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" means the trap fired with the wrong wording.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"What it costs, and when to spend it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each call is a child process — some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"60 ms, against 1 ms for an in-process assertion. This is the decision point,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the rule lives here and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TestingYourGame.md"},{"type":"text","text":" points at it. A trap wants"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one of three shapes, in the order they are worth reaching for; only the last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"of them is this function:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the bad message unrepresentable, and write no test at all."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a group of traps shares a sentence, fold them into one helper that derives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole of it — or at least takes the missing half as a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"required","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"argument — so the next call site cannot omit or contradict it. Where a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trap guards an argument no caller could sensibly mean, change the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"signature so the compiler refuses it. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HolderTrait"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"declaredFuse(_:in:else:)"},{"text":" are the first; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"oneOf(_:_:)"},{"text":" is the second.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"A pure function, asserted in process","type":"text"}]},{"text":", for an ordinary precondition, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose message has branches worth checking apiece. Split the message","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out and test it at a millisecond — the shape ","type":"text"},{"code":"Reentry.diagnostic(depth:entity:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"TraitKey.diagnostic(for:of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" use."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An exit test","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — this function — where the trap’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"wording","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is what an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"author will read to find their mistake and no pure function can stand in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the run, or where a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"margin","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" only a real run can measure is at stake.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An entity built inside a rule body; ","type":"text"},{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" read on the opening look; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"scoring register the award table does not list; a cap that has to fire"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the stack does."}]}]}]}]}],"references":{"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport":{"title":"GnustoTestSupport","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Boot a game, feed it the commands a player would type, and assert on what it printed."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport","role":"collection"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"expectTrap","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExitTest","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing8ExitTestV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing8ExitTestV6ResultV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"says"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"..., "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","precise